# Lesson 5: Patterns
# NOW categories start to emerge. Not because we told Ada
# "cat is an animal." Because she already knows cat has fur,
# cat has legs, cat can run, dog has fur, dog has legs, dog
# can run — and she notices the PATTERN.
#
# This lesson gives names to patterns she's already seen.

# --- Naming the patterns ---
cat is_a animal
dog is_a animal
mom is_a person
dad is_a person
a is_a letter
b is_a letter
c is_a letter
red is_a color
big is_a size
hot is_a temperature
cold is_a temperature
happy is_a feeling
sad is_a feeling
home is_a place

# --- Properties of categories ---
animal has fur
animal has legs
animal can run
animal can eat
person has name
person has eyes
person can run
person can eat
letter says sound
color is visual
feeling is inside

# --- Now she can INFER ---
# She wasn't told "cat is visual" but:
# cat has fur → animal has fur → she knows what animal means
# She wasn't told "mom can eat" but:
# mom is_a person → person can eat → inference
